<!--
  =====================================================================
  launchd agent for MBY-Trading.

  INSTALL

    1. Edit the two paths marked EDIT ME below to your project folder.
    2. cp scripts/com.mby.trading.desk.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    3. launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mby.trading.desk.plist 2>/dev/null
       launchctl load  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mby.trading.desk.plist
    4. launchctl list | grep com.mby     # confirm it is registered

  To stop it:
       launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mby.trading.desk.plist

  WHY EVERY FIFTEEN MINUTES AND NOT THREE FIXED TIMES

  launchd fires on LOCAL time and gives no way to say "09:45 New York".
  Three fixed local times would be an hour wrong for several weeks a
  year — the US and Europe change clocks on different dates, and much
  of West Africa never changes at all — and being an hour wrong means
  either trading into a closed market or missing the session entirely.

  So this ticks every fifteen minutes and `orchestrator auto` reads the
  Eastern clock itself, decides whether anything is due, checks whether
  it already ran, and almost always exits immediately having done
  nothing. Correct across every DST boundary with no maintenance, and a
  tick missed because the machine was asleep is picked up by the next
  one instead of losing the day.

  RunAtLoad is true for the same reason: a laptop opened at 10:15 runs
  the execution group it slept through, rather than waiting for the
  next quarter hour.

  THE ONE THING THIS CANNOT DO is run while the machine is asleep or
  shut. A closed laptop is a desk that does not trade. If unattended
  operation needs to survive that, the same wrapper belongs on an
  always-on host — a small VPS or the Railway deployment the
  orchestrator was originally written for — and the plist is then
  replaced by that host's cron.
  =====================================================================
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.mby.trading.desk</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <!-- EDIT ME -->
        <string>/Users/malickmbaye_1/Downloads/ai_trading_firm 6/scripts/run_desk.sh</string>
        <string>auto</string>
    </array>

    <!-- EDIT ME -->
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/malickmbaye_1/Downloads/ai_trading_firm 6</string>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>900</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
      Docker Desktop lives in /usr/local/bin or /opt/homebrew/bin
      depending on the Mac. launchd's default PATH contains neither, and
      the wrapper needs `docker` to bring the database up after a sleep.
    -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <!--
      The wrapper writes its own dated log; these two catch anything
      that fails before it gets that far — a bad path, a missing shell,
      a permissions problem. That is exactly the class of failure that
      otherwise leaves no trace at all.
    -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/mby-desk.launchd.out</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/mby-desk.launchd.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
